# Replay instructions

The portable replay executes the 19 accepted producer scripts in dependency
order. The superseded C4-only q-transfer script is retained in `rejected/` and
is not executed.

```bash
PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 replay.py --check
```

The replay regenerates the JSON files under `results/` and compares their
SHA-256 hashes against `EXPECTED_RESULTS.sha256`.

Dependencies used by the scripts are standard Python plus `numpy`, `scipy`, and
`mpmath`. No network access is used.

A successful replay establishes reproducibility of this implementation, not
formal-proof-assistant verification or empirical validation.
